## Proposed fix

Either split the long interaction chain (the test fills several antd fields through `userEvent` before the assertion) into two tests, or give this one test an explicit timeout as the `IncidentsPanel` Popconfirm tests already do (`}, 15000);`). Prefer the split: the timeout only moves the cliff.

## Repro

```bash
cd frontend
npx vitest run --coverage --coverage.thresholds.lines=0 tests/components/ConnectionForm.test.tsx
```
Second data point, same file, different test: with the backend suite running concurrently on the same machine, `tests/components/ConnectionForm.test.tsx › a service principal swaps the user for tenant + client ids and a client secret` timed out at 5023 ms (and the SQL Server test at 5047 ms in an earlier run). Both pass with the machine idle (the full `vitest run` is green at 1770 tests). So the margin is file-wide, not one test: every ConnectionForm case that opens the type select and fills several fields sits close to the 5 s default under load. Raising the per-file timeout (or splitting the heaviest cases) is the fix shape, rather than touching the two cases that happened to cross first.

